From: Randall <randall@rpx.io>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: rsinput: declare FF_SINE alongside FF_PERIODIC

The rumble bridge declares FF_PERIODIC but no waveform bit, so ff-core
rejects any direct periodic upload with EINVAL before the driver sees it
(fftest effect 0). The qcom-hv-haptics driver already accepts FF_SINE.
Declare it. FF_RUMBLE is unaffected: ff-core adds it for every device
that declares FF_PERIODIC and converts it to a sine internally.

---
diff --git a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
index d3369da..cbf4d8d 100644
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
@@ -640,6 +640,13 @@ static int rsinput_probe(struct serdev_device *serdev) {
         input_set_drvdata(drv->input, drv);
         INIT_WORK(&drv->rumble_work, rsinput_rumble_work);
         input_set_capability(drv->input, EV_FF, FF_PERIODIC);
+        /*
+         * ff-core rejects a periodic upload whose waveform bit is not set
+         * before the driver sees it. The haptics driver handles FF_SINE
+         * (patch 1001), so declare it; FF_RUMBLE keeps working because
+         * ff-core adds it for any device that declares FF_PERIODIC.
+         */
+        input_set_capability(drv->input, EV_FF, FF_SINE);
 
         error = input_ff_create(drv->input, 1);
         if (error) {
